    "roles": ["band_member", "touring", "producer"],
    "summary": "Khruangbin's drummer: a Houston musician who started on drums at two or three, after his uncle John Foster, moved to the organ in his late teens and played it in Rudy Rasmus's gospel band at St. John's, where he met Mark Speer. Asked to join Speer and Laura Lee's trio to play \"simple break-beats\", he came back to the kit. On a small jazz kit with one floor tom and a piccolo snare damped with a strip of leather, he plays breakbeats mimicked \"down to the tone of the drum\", sixteenths or eighths on the hat, hardly a fill and never to a click. Half of the Houston hip-hop production duo Beanz N Kornbread."
  },
